mutant: m075_sparse_collection_count_stale
target: segment/sparse.go
failure-mode: |
  The sparse rewrite keeps the source's per-collection event counts
  instead of reducing them by the dropped rows (design §12.2 step 5). The
  new generation's collection index over-reports, and a collection whose
  rows were all deleted is never removed from the string table, so
  collection-filtered planning keeps fetching blocks with nothing to
  serve.
expected-detection: |
  The layer 3 oracle's held reader runs segment.VerifySealedMetadata on
  every generation it sees while current, which recounts each
  collection's rows. TestSparseRewriteMatchesRewrite catches it at unit
  level.
expected-tier: disagg
tiers: disagg

diff --git a/segment/sparse.go b/segment/sparse.go
index c33056b..52d873e 100644
--- a/segment/sparse.go
+++ b/segment/sparse.go
@@ -558,7 +558,6 @@ func (s *sparseRewrite) collectionIndex() ([]byte, error) {
 			return nil, fmt.Errorf("%w: %s drops %d rows of collection %q, footer counts %d",
 				ErrInvalidFooter, s.opts.Name, n, name, counts[id])
 		}
-		counts[id] -= n
 	}
 
 	bitmasks := make([][]uint32, len(s.blocks))
